  "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch of factor $3$ and invariant $y$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch of factor $4$ and invariant $x$-axis can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,4y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(3x,4y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(-2,3)↦(3\\cdot (-2),\\,4\\cdot 3)=(-6,12).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275005/assets/021d6f83d9964d84476ebc1916e1d58038016dfbee60237c81a74faa30b95ee6.png)",
